    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation for `POST /api/owners`: a request carrying an `Idempotency-Key` header that repeats an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise be a 409 household-duplicate conflict).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (no `@RestController`), I added:\n\n**New function classes** (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a Spring `@Component` singleton mapping each seen key \u2192 created owner id.\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 the new **first** step. Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header via `ServerHttpConnection` (case-insensitive `getHeader`, and `null`-safe when absent so ordinary creates are unaffected). If the key was seen, it re-loads the original owner and takes the `existing` branch; otherwise the `proceed` branch runs the normal pipeline. It reads only the header, never the body, so `validate` remains the sole `@RequestBody` binder. It republishes the key as a variable.\n- `RecordIdempotency` \u2014 runs after `save` (so the id exists) and associates the key with the created owner; a keyless request is a no-op.\n- `Continuation` \u2014 a `@FunctionalInterface` used for the two `@Flow` branch outputs.\n\n**Reused** `RespondWithOwner` (an existing 200 responder) for the replay branch.\n\n**YAML** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`): added `checkIdempotency` as the entry step with conditional `outputs: { proceed: validate, existing: respondExisting }` (no `next:`, so exactly one branch runs), inserted `record` between `save` and `audit`, and added the `respondExisting` step. All new steps carry `govern: [ transaction ]` to stay within the endpoint's single transaction.\n\nHow I verified the framework specifics (headers, `@Flow` outputs, first-step-is-entry) rather than guessing: I inspected the OfficeFloor library sources in the local `~/.m2` (`officeweb`, `officeserver`, `officecompose`, the spring-boot starter) to confirm `ServerHttpConnection.getRequest().getHeaders().getHeader(...)` is case-insensitive, that `@Flow(\"name\")` maps to an `outputs:` branch name, and that the first YAML function becomes the endpoint entry point.\n\nResults: `AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` build succeeds (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
