    "probe_text": "The endpoint is served entirely by an OfficeFloor pipeline (`src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 there is no Spring `@RestController`. Here is the full ordered sequence, all running inside a single `transaction` governance (any escalation rolls back before persistence).\n\n## Pre-checks / gate\n\n1. **Authorization** (`composition.authorize`) \u2014 `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` guards the whole file. (Note: `petclinic.security.enable=false` in `application.properties` disables it by default.)\n2. **Idempotency check** (`CheckIdempotencyKey`) \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header (not the body). If the key was already seen, it reloads the prior owner and short-circuits to `respondExisting` \u2192 **200** with the original owner (no validation, no checks, no insert). Otherwise it republishes the key and proceeds.\n\n## Validations (each can reject; `ValidateOwnerFields` collects all field errors \u2192 **400** `OwnerFieldsInvalidException`)\n\n3. **Required non-blank fields** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`.\n4. **Address** \u2014 normalized via `AddressFields.normalizeInto` (prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` over flat `address`); neither present \u2192 error. *(Side-effect: writes normalized/canonical address back onto the request.)*\n5. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** \u2014 normalized via `TelephoneE164.toE164`; unparseable \u2192 error. *(Side-effect: overwrites `telephone` with the E.164 form.)*\n6. **Email** (optional) \u2014 must match the email regex and not be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); invalid \u2192 error. *(Side-effect: stored trimmed + lower-cased.)*\n7. **Postcode** (optional) \u2014 must be a 4-digit value valid for the city (`Postcode.isValidForCity`); invalid \u2192 error. *(Side-effect: stored trimmed.)*\n8. **Registration date** (optional) \u2014 must not be in the future; else error.\n9. **City capacity** (`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`) \u2014 rejects with **409** `OwnerCityAtCapacityException` if the city already has \u2265 50 owners.\n10. **Daily limit** (`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`) \u2014 rejects with **429** `OwnerDailyLimitExceededException` if \u2265 100 owners already registered for the business day.\n\n## Build & derived-field assignment (mutations, before save)\n\n11. **Build owner** (`BuildOwner`) \u2014 MapStruct `toOwner`; defaults `registrationDate` to today and rolls it to a business day (`BusinessDay.adjust`).\n12. **Assign household** (`AssignHousehold`) \u2014 `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode`.\n13. **Household-identity uniqueness** (`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`) \u2014 rejects with **409** `OwnerIdentityConflictException` if a non-deleted owner shares the `householdId`, unless the request opted in via `sharesHousehold`. *(This is a validation, placed after the id is derived and before save.)*\n14. **Assign household size** (`AssignHouseholdSize`) \u2014 existing housemates + 1.\n15. **Assign customer code** (`AssignCustomerCode`) \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, de-duplicated with a `-<n>` suffix.\n16. **Assign namesake count** (`AssignNamesakeCount`) \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name.\n17. **Assign bulk-signup warning** (`AssignBulkSignupWarning`) \u2014 true if > 80 owners already registered that business day.\n18. **Assign possible-duplicate flags** (`AssignPossibleDuplicate`) \u2014 soft-match: flags `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when an existing non-deleted owner shares lastName+postcode but has a different telephone (skipped for declared household members).\n\n## Persistence & post-save side-effects\n\n19. **Save** (`SaveOwner`) \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (the only DB insert).\n20. **Record idempotency** (`RecordIdempotency`) \u2014 associates the `Idempotency-Key` with the new owner id (no-op if no key was supplied).\n21. **Audit** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` SLF4J log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber).\n22. **Respond** (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nNote the entity/DTO bean-validation annotations (`@NotEmpty`, `@Pattern`, `@Email`, etc.) are **not** the enforcement path here \u2014 the OfficeFloor binder does not run bean validation, so all request validation is the manual logic in `ValidateOwnerFields` and the check steps above."
